--- a/start/README.md
+++ b/result/README.md
@@ -33,6 +33,26 @@ happened. Its own staff work in the organization as members with roles. Go stand
   through them. `next_cursor` is absent on the last page.
 - Times are RFC 3339 in UTC. Amounts are integers in the currency's minor unit; fields ending in `_formatted` are for people.
 - Every response carries an `X-Request-Id` (the caller's, when it sent a sensible one).
+- A member whose role may not use an endpoint gets 403 `forbidden` and nothing changes. The role is read on every request.
+
+### Roles
+
+| What | owner | admin | billing | member | viewer |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Read customers, plans, subscriptions, invoices, payments | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |
+| Create, update or delete customers | yes | yes | yes | yes | no |
+| Create or update plans | yes | yes | yes | no | no |
+| Create, update or cancel subscriptions; report usage | yes | yes | yes | yes | no |
+| Create, pay or void invoices; revenue report | yes | yes | yes | no | no |
+| Webhook endpoints, deliveries and events | yes | yes | no | no | no |
+| Read the organization, members and invites | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |
+| Update the organization; invite, revoke invites, change roles, remove members | yes | yes | no | no | no |
+
+- Only an owner gives the owner or admin role, changes the role of, or removes, an owner or an admin.
+- Nobody changes their own role. Anyone may leave (`DELETE /v1/members/{their own user_id}`).
+- An organization keeps at least one owner: a change that would leave none is 409 `last_owner`.
+- Every member may create API keys and revoke their own. Owners and admins may revoke anyone's. `GET /v1/api-keys` lists the
+  whole organization's keys for owners and admins, and only the caller's own for everyone else.
 
 ## Working on Tally
 
